✅ 5.Can we start the same thread twice?

Example:

thread.start();
thread.start();

Result:
java.lang.IllegalThreadStateException

Internal Flow

NEW
 | start()
 ▼
RUNNABLE
 |
 ▼
TERMINATED
 | start() again
 ▼
IllegalThreadStateException

Reason:

🔴 A Thread object represents one independent execution.
🔴 Once start() is called, the thread transitions from NEW to RUNNABLE.
🔴 After the run() method completes, the thread enters the TERMINATED state.
🔴 A thread cannot transition back to the NEW state, so it cannot be started again.